  "term": "creationism",
  "definition": "Creationism is a religious-philosophical view that the world was brought into being by a Creator who remains distinct from the universe rather than being identical with it. In this historical sense, it may refer either to a single creative act or to ongoing creation through a series of acts, while still emphasizing the Creator’s transcendence.",
